ZPlanKit changelog

1.41.2 (2026-11-12)
  Planner (czplan.c), Fix v18.4: stop depths on whole multiples of the stop
  distance. 1.39.0 built the grid up from the last stop, so a 4.5 m last
  stop with 3 m stops gave 16.5, 13.5, 10.5, 7.5, 4.5. Stops are now the
  multiples of the stop distance deeper than the last stop, then the last
  stop: 15, 12, 9, 6, 4.5 (imperial 50, 40, 30, 20, 15 ft). A diver who
  cannot leave the last stop stays there. Last stops that are a multiple of
  the stop distance (3, 6, 9 m; 10, 20, 30 ft) are unchanged in every model
  (680-plan comparison with 1.41.1, vval79_check 163/263/326, emc20h_check
  PASS). Apps: Lplanner 1.11.1 (11) macOS/iOS, 1.11.1 (21) Android.

1.41.1 (2026-11-10)
  Planner (czplan.c), from Audit v18.0:
  - VVAL-79 at altitude: Cross correction, as in the U.S. Navy Diving Manual.
    Before, the tolerated pressure was p_surface + (Pt - MPTT0) and the
    schedule got shorter with altitude (30 m 40 min air: 26, 11, 2, 0 min at
    0, 1500, 2500, 3500 m). Now the model runs on P k, k = P_sea / P_site:
    tolerated P = (P_sea + (Pt - MPTT0)) / k, stops at the sea-level stop
    depths divided by k, equilibrated tissues at the sea-level tension, a
    diver just arrived at k times it. Same dive: 26, 51, 70, 95 min. The plan
    is identical to the sea-level plan for the sea level equivalent depth
    (checked on 24 dives) and carries a note. The exact pressure ratio is
    used, not the 1,000 ft bands and rounded depths of Table 9-4. Tissue
    files hold actual tensions as before.
  - Time to Fly, VVAL-79: washout with the Thalmann half-times (was the
    Buhlmann table by index; 12 m 300 min air 2.5 h, now 4.5 h).
  - Time to Fly, gradient factors: always GF High. A no-stop dive could be
    tested against GF Low (10 m 200 min at GF 30/85: 37.5 h, now 3.0 h).
  Sea-level schedules of every model are unchanged (144-plan comparison with
  1.41.0, vval79_check 163/263/326, emc20h_check PASS).

1.41.0 (2026-11-10)
  Planner (czplan.c): three U.S. Navy exact models, run as the NEDU table
  programs run them.
  - Model: XVal-He-4B (NEDU TR 10-04), XVal-He-4 (NEDU TR 02-10),
    VVAL-18 air (NEDU TR 07-09); short forms xhe4b, xhe4, vval18.
  - Thalmann EL-DCM in fsw with 33 fsw/atm: P_I = (1 - FO2) P - 1.5,
    X = P - 4.3, exponential uptake, linear washout above X, helium and
    nitrogen summed, no tension floor. Closed circuit FO2 = min(SP 33 / P, 1),
    SP in ata. Depths are converted with 1 ft = 1 fsw.
  - Leave a stop when T_i <= b_i + s_i x for every compartment, x the next
    stop depth (0 from the last stop). Stops in whole minutes, travel
    excluded; each second of travel loads at the depth reached.
  - XVal-He-4B: 8 compartments (10-240 min); XVal-He-4: 9 (5-240 min);
    VVAL-18: 9, MPTT 120 ... 43.5, slope 1.
  - A stop that does not clear within 600 min refuses the plan (XVal-He-4
    deeper than about 210 fsw). Altitude refused. VVAL-18 refuses helium.
    A tissue file without U.S. Navy tensions refuses a repetitive dive.
  - Warning when an XVal-He plan is outside the MK 16 MOD 1 validation
    (1.3 atm PO2 heliox, 200 fsw).
  - Gradient factors, Pyle stops and Conservatism do not apply.
  - Repetitive dives: the tissue file carries a "NAVY:" line of 9 tensions
    (fsw), written and read by zp_emc_tissue_line / zp_read_emc_tissue_line;
    the surface interval is run on air with the same kinetics.
  - Altitude after diving: Method 1 unavailable for these models.
  New key SetpointUnit: bar (default) or ata, for every model. Waypoint
  setpoints, slide maxima, DecoSetpoint and SlideRate are read in that unit
  and held in bar; each model converts what it needs (VVAL-79 and the Navy
  models work in ata, EMC-20H in atm, ZHL-16C and VPM-B in bar). The report
  prints "CCR setpoints in bar/ata" above a closed-circuit schedule, and the
  SP and PO2 of closed-circuit rows in that unit. Before, VVAL-79 read the
  setpoint as ata and the other models as bar. With SetpointUnit: bar,
  ZHL-16C, VPM-B and EMC-20H plans are unchanged; with ata, VVAL-79 and the
  Navy models are unchanged.
  Checked against the NavyBench engine (vval18he_tester v16.9 plan_navy):
  2,712 imperial dives (40-300 fsw, 10-90 min, CCR heliox, CCR trimix, OC
  trimix with EAN50 and O2, air and nitrox, last stop 10 and 20 fsw):
  2,704 identical, including all 296 plans with no schedule. The other 8
  differ only in when EAN50 is first breathed when the bottom is shallower
  than its switch depth (the planner switches at the next stop depth).
  ZHL-16C, VVAL-79, VPM-B and EMC-20H: 3,584 reports identical to 1.40.0.
  Reference/navy_check.sh against the 231 MK 16 MOD 1 schedules of NEDU
  TR 02-10 Appendix J (60-200 fsw): XVal-He-4 228 within 1 min (worst
  1.3), XVal-He-4B 219 within 1 min (worst 7.0 at 190-200 fsw, the dropped
  1-minute deep stops TR 10-04 describes).

1.40.0 (2026-10-27)
  Planner (czplan.c): new model, Model: emc20h (also emc, cochran).
  - Cochran EMC-20H: 20 compartments in equivalent-air-depth units, one
    combined inert tension, exact uptake and first-order washout per second,
    nitrogen and helium limits blended by the gas breathed, stop rule
    T <= M + (1 - FO2) F X / 0.79, depth factor
    F = (1 + W + Tc)(1 - 0.0175 min(n,30)) + C/200 + 26/512 with the
    deep-stop credit earned from a first-stop projection every second.
  - New keys: WaterTemp (C metric, F imperial), TempComp off/low/high,
    Workload (L/min; default nominal 5/256). Conservatism feeds C/200.
  - Stops are held to the second, not rounded to the minute. Pyle deep
    stops and gradient factors are off for this model. Altitude refused.
  - Repetitive dives: the tissue file carries an "EMC:" line of 20 tensions;
    zp_emc_tissue_line / zp_read_emc_tissue_line write and read it. Surface
    interval once per minute, T <- T (1 - 1/half-time).
  - Time to fly and altitude Method 1 keep using the parallel ZHL-16C
    tissues; Method 1 is reported unavailable for EMC-20H plans.
  Reference: emc20h_check.sh against 70 Analyst plans, mean |total
  difference| 0.16 min, largest 0.55 min.
  VVAL-79: last stop now follows the VVal-79 parameter LST_DOMode = 1
  (NEDU TR 12-01 Table B.2): the last stop is left when the tensions at
  that stop are within the surfacing MPTTs, with no credit for the ascent
  to the next stop increment. Changes only plans whose last stop is deeper
  than the stop distance (e.g. a 20 ft last stop). can_surface_from_increment
  removed. Against the 383 VVal-79 air schedules of TR 12-01 Appendix E:
  exact 83 -> 163, within 1 min 213 -> 263, bias -1.69 -> -1.11 min
  (Reference/vval79_check.sh).
  Regression set unchanged (ZHL-16C 80, VVAL-79 8, VPM-B).

1.39.3 (2026-10-09)
  Planner (czplan.c):
  - The EAD column honours O2 narcotic. On a helium mix it prints the END
    (oxygen counted when O2 narcotic is on); on a helium-free mix it stays
    the nitrogen-only EAD, as MultiDeco does. Before, the column was always
    nitrogen-only: 90 m on 11/57 with O2 narcotic on printed 30 m, not 33 m.
  - A GasSw row is printed only when no stop follows at the switch depth.
    When there is one, the stop row carries the new gas: 21 m EAN50 and
    9 m EAN80 now print once instead of a 0:00 GasSw row plus the stop.
    Stop list, run time, CNS, OTU and gas totals unchanged.
  Regression set unchanged (ZHL-16C 80, VVAL-79 8, VPM-B).
  Copied to Lplanner-FDroid/engine (was 1.39.0). Lplanner-Android compiles
  this checkout directly. Both apps 1.9.2.

1.39.2 (2026-10-08)
  Planner (czplan.c):
  - Waypoint profiles are now checked against the ceiling. Waypoints are
    still flown exactly as entered and no stops are added between them,
    but when an ascent between waypoints breaks the ceiling the report
    warns, naming the leg and how far it went:
      ZHL-16C: the highest GF reached, against GF high (100% without GF).
      VVAL-79: metres above the ceiling.
    VPM-B is not checked yet.
    A tester entered 90 m / 20 min on 11/57 followed by stops at 36, 18, 9
    and 6 m as waypoints. The plan came out with no warning, yet the leg
    from 18 to 9 m reaches GF 250% against GF high 87%.
    Regression set unchanged (ZHL-16C, VVAL-79 and VPM-B).
  The vendored engine copies in Lplanner-Android and Lplanner-FDroid are
  not updated.

1.39.1 (2026-09-29)
  Planner (czplan.c):
  - During the ascent the gas and setpoint are now checked at every grid
    depth, including depths where no stop is needed. The switch is made on
    the fly at the switch depth, so the diver reaches the next stop already
    on the new gas. Before, the check waited for a stop: 45 m / 20 min air
    at GF 20/95 with EAN50 switched at 18 m instead of 21 m.
    Stop lists unchanged over the regression set; CNS and OTU rise slightly
    on 4 of 96 rows because the switch comes earlier.
  The vendored engine copies in Lplanner-Android and Lplanner-FDroid are
  not updated.
  The dive computer engine (zp_rt) lives in its own repository,
  DiveComputerEngine, next to this one.
